00:49:21.670 --> 00:49:30.000
Well, I don't really consider myself being at the center of Fleetwood Mac in some ways,

00:49:30.000 --> 00:49:36.900
I mean, as a stabilizing figure, then that was definitely the case.

00:49:37.160 --> 00:49:44.210
In terms of being visible, I think speaking for myself and John,

00:49:44.350 --> 00:49:51.110
I look at myself as someone who plays the drums for other people.

00:49:52.420 --> 00:50:00.000
The other people, you know, other people that are there to be complimented by Mick,

00:50:00.600 --> 00:50:16.750
the drummer, musician, person that's hard to pin down, hard to describe, if you like.

00:50:16.750 --> 00:50:25.590
I think Stevie gets blamed, probably, because she's a very visible, blamed for, you know,

00:50:25.590 --> 00:50:26.590
causing problems.

00:50:26.590 --> 00:50:30.000
I mean, she's the most visible entity.

00:50:30.000 --> 00:50:39.180
of going out and being tremendously successful in her own right as a performer and as a writer

00:50:39.180 --> 00:50:50.380
and everything else. The bad girl image is, I suppose, revolves around that, you know,

00:50:50.380 --> 00:50:58.390
but it's really nothing as sinister as that, I don't think.

